  "summary": "The audit checks the 81 units: the six HumBio core courses (HUMBIO 2A, 2B, 3A, 3B, 4A and 4B, letter graded), one statistics course (letter graded), three upper-division HumBio or listed Overseas Studies courses, the WIM (the B-side core courses) and one capstone option. Every letter-graded course needs a C- or better. Two upper-division courses must be letter graded and the third may be CR/NC, 9 units in all; the exception that moves the CR/NC allowance to a Depth course is checked by hand. Checked by hand: the 20 units of breadth and five depth courses approved by the HumBio advising team (the audit checks that a moved-in depth course is letter graded and 3 or more units; three departments are checked by hand), the BA-designated courses, Interdisciplinary Honors, the non-PWR Notation elective, and transfer credit, which has its own limits per requirement.",
